\newlabel{tab:shrinkage}{{4}{16}{Effect of empirical-Bayes shrinkage on the tail-risk ranking. $p_i^{\mathrm {raw}}$ and $p_i^{\mathrm {EB}}$ are the raw and shrunk conditional probabilities $p_i(0.95)$; $T_i$ is the number of tourism upper-tail events. Municipalities with few events are pulled toward the regional baseline $0.116$ and drop in rank}{table.caption.16}{}}
